#{[#edb/ref 17592186055061 "$$\n{{\\overset{P}{\\overset{⏞}{{3}^{2}=9}}\\,\\overset{∧}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{and}}}\\,\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{2\\text{ is rational}}}}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∧\\,Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is irrational}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P∧Q$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $(P∧Q)∧R$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 13194139535324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [#edb/ref 17592186055087 "$$\n{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 13194139536086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [#edb/ref 17592186055088 "$$\n{{2\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\overset{S}{\\overset{⏞}{7\\,|\\,14}}\\,\\overset{∧}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{and}}}\\,\\overset{T}{\\overset{⏞}{5\\,|\\,14}}}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∧\\,T}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $S∧T$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $R∨(S∧T)$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 13194139533456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [#edb/ref 17592186120080 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{1}?$" #edb/ref 13194139535468 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186120185 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$, given by\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(L)\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(U), b = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$.\nIf $⟨x_{1}, x_{2}⟩$ and $⟨y_{1}, y_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax = b$ and $Ly = b$ respectively, what is the value of $x_{1} \\cdot y_{2}$?" #edb/ref 13194139533360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [#edb/ref 17592186120205 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" #edb/ref 13194139535468 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186120206 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" #edb/ref 13194139535468 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186120208 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 12 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 7 & -12\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -17\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" #edb/ref 13194139535468 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186204214 "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a,b\\in Z,$ if $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,20),$ then $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,20).$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}(\\text{mod}\\,20)\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-5}}(\\text{mod}\\,20).\n$$\n\nLet's choose\n\n$$\na={{field-6}},\\,b={{field-7}}.\n$$\n\nThen, $5a=$ {{field-8}} and $5b=$ {{field-9}}. \n\nHence, we have that \n\n$$\n{{20}_{⏟}}_{5a}{{field-10}}{{40}_{⏟}}_{5b}\\,(\\text{mod}\\,20)\\,\\text{and}\\,{{4}_{⏟}}_{a}{{field-11}}{{8}_{⏟}}_{b}\\,(\\text{mod}\\,20).\n$$\n\nSo, the pair $a=$ {{field-12}} and $b=$ {{field-13}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." #edb/ref 13194139534331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [#edb/ref 17592186224995 "What is the positive solution to the equation $4y^2 - 17y - 15 = 0$?\n\nExplanation:\n\nTo factor the left-hand side, we need two numbers that multiply to $4 \\cdot (-15) = -60$ and add to $-17$. These two numbers are $-20$ and $3$, so we can factor the left-hand side as follows:\n\n$4y^{2} - 17y - 15|= 0; 4y^{2}- 20y + 3y_(⏟)_(-17y) - 15|= 0; 4y(y - 5) + 3(y - 5)|= 0; (y - 5)(4y + 3)|= 0$\n\nApplying the zero product rule, we have the following:\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}y - 5 = 0 & ⇒y = 5 \\\\ 4y + 3 = 0 & ⇒y =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the **positive** solution to the given equation is $y = 5$." #edb/ref 13194139533383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [#edb/ref 17592186240947 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions of the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of the product ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186241076 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186241077 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186241084 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -10 \\\\ 4 & 6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186241086 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186241146 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186241147 "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186243989 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 63 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} & \\boxed{} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. From left to right, what are the missing elements from the second row of the matrix $U?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186243990 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186243991 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{31}$ in the matrix $L?$" #edb/ref 13194139535475 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [#edb/ref 17592186243992 "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 3 \\